":"awards_nominees","name":"Best Cinematography","nominee_list":[{"type":"movie","id":335984,"name":"Blade Runner 2049","image_path":"/jLul37v1NcF8XpdSEh4RHsmGocA.jpg","director":"Denis Villeneuve","winner":true},{"type":"movie","id":399055,"name":"The Shape of Water","image_path":"/hHPFq7myTjAVH6CwQjamAuUqhrr.jpg","director":"Guillermo del Toro","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":399404,"name":"Darkest Hour","image_path":"/mvB7rx0RwwRWweO05CbDU5T5c5a.jpg","director":"Joe Wright","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":374720,"name":"Dunkirk","image_path":"/8TbAQlEpRG2EQsjMNR76IYGNuki.jpg","director":"Christopher Nolan","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":414425,"name":"Mudbound","image_path":"/1jmobU7W4G25dMHCanyaihTsUmh.jpg","director":"Dee Rees","winner":false}]},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Best Director","nominee_list":[{"type":"person","id":10828,"image_path":"/gldeyCtKcaqnK1v4Vu9vqayhzUQ.jpg","name":"Guillermo del Toro","winner":true,"movie":{"type":"movie","id":399055,"name":"The Shape of Water","image_path":"/hHPFq7myTjAVH6CwQjamAuUqhrr.jpg","director":"Guillermo del Toro","winner":true}},{"type":"person","id":525,"image_path":"/xuAIuYSmsUzKlUMBFGVZaWsY3DZ.jpg","name":"Christopher Nolan","winner":false,"movie":{"type":"movie","id":374720,"name":"Dunkirk","image_path":"/8TbAQlEpRG2EQsjMNR76IYGNuki.jpg","director":"Christopher Nolan","winner":false}},{"type":"person","id":4762,"image_path":"/29DHpRKddqTwo2NU162Y49JoQYa.jpg","name":"Paul Thomas Anderson","winner":false,"movie":{"type":"movie","id":400617,"name":"Phantom Thread","image_path":"/tNbAIYx1dDX2WXrwUxQuMziiSTD.jpg","director":"Paul Thomas Anderson","winner":false}},{"type":"person","id":291263,"image_path":"/9rOEfvKUInuUpJ6MMhiC8Tch1WM.jpg","name":"Jordan Peele","winner":false,"movie":{"type":"movie","id":419430,"name":"Get Out","image_path":"/A0RoSZh8PEYJgDMgM2EV7Ycz3dR.jpg","director":"Jordan Peele","winner":false}},{"type":"person","id":45400,"image_path":"/3H0xzU12GTNJyQTpGysEuI9KyiQ.jpg","name":"\"Greta Gerwig","winner":false,"movie":{"type":"movie","id":391713,"name":"Lady Bird","image_path":"/wxfKcpFPmK9isnxXyvCMbqmBtdg.jpg","director":"Greta Gerwig","winner":false}}]},{"type":"block_special","title":"Retrospective Assessment and Ratings","description":"The 2018 edition received mixed reviews from television and film critics. The main point of analysis was Jimmy Kimmel's moderate, restrained hosting. Hank Stuever, a journalist at The Washington Post, commented that \"in his second year, Kimmel showed that the broadcast doesn't need to be anything other than crisp and confident, with an entertaining pace [...] we [viewers] have no pretension of making entertainment industry history, we just want to watch another Oscar night.\" David Edelstein, chief critic at New York Magazine, opined: \"this was the best, most inspiring and most likable broadcast of the ceremony I have watched; but, on the other hand, it was also, in terms of the awards, one of the most disappointing.\" Richard Lawson of Vanity Fair noted that \"as host, Kimmel struck a careful, meticulously calculated tone... Sunday night did an admirable job of acknowledging all the political turmoil surrounding it.\" CNN critic Brian Lowry said that \"the Oscars are a big mess that clumsily tries to congratulate the truly deserving; however, if the intention was ultimately not to ignore the outside world and to serve society, Kimmel and the Academy did very well.\"<br/><br/>\n\nOther figures, on the other hand, gave the ceremony negative reviews. Television critic Maureen Ryan of Variety commented: \"taking the show as a whole, I felt a more or less low vibe. Usually, two hours into the broadcast the numbing effect sets in, but despite host Kimmel's efforts, this edition was languid, lacking energy.\" James Poniewozik of The New York Times: \"despite the recent upheaval in Hollywood, the ceremony largely focused on celebrating film.\" Columnist Kristi Turnquist of The Oregonian commented: \"it was utterly respectful, a formal and dull kind of ceremony.\" <br/><br/>\n\nAccording to Nielsen Ratings, the ABC broadcast drew 26.5 million viewers in the United States, 19% fewer than the previous ceremony, making the 2018 edition the least-watched in Oscar history."},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Best Costume Design","nominee_list":[{"type":"movie","id":400617,"name":"Phantom Thread","image_path":"/tNbAIYx1dDX2WXrwUxQuMziiSTD.jpg","director":"Paul Thomas Anderson","winner":true},{"type":"movie","id":399055,"name":"The Shape of Water","image_path":"/hHPFq7myTjAVH6CwQjamAuUqhrr.jpg","director":"Guillermo del Toro","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":399404,"name":"Darkest Hour","image_path":"/mvB7rx0RwwRWweO05CbDU5T5c5a.jpg","director":"Joe Wright","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":321612,"name":"Beauty and the Beast","image_path":"/9V4wl4rnUcLfGuTe4J5NjOFbDil.jpg","director":"Bill Condon","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":423899,"name":"Victoria & Abdul","image_path":"/sIgzpUqe31wUjiFJ5gSucbFAekP.jpg","director":"Stephen Frears","winner":false}]},{"type":"video","video_id":"4gU6CpQk6BE","information":{"contentTitle":"Frances McDormand wins Best Actress","source":"YouTube: <i>Oscar</i> channel"}},{"type":"awards_nominees","name":"Best Documentary Feature","nominee_list":[{"type":"movie","id":566285,"name":"Ícaro","image_path":"/p8mBFFwPXBYrM58iJ4DK6oENbFx.jpg","director":"Arthur Padilha","winner":true},{"type":"movie","id":411007,"name":"Abacus: Small Enough to Jail","image_path":"/4u00FWfh8dUruEB7C3KCaV3FtOH.jpg","director":"Steve James","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":451995,"name":"Faces Places","image_path":"/mSOda2XtnrupIb5g0vqyEWbL3AO.jpg","director":"JR e Agnès Varda","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":433085,"name":"Last Men in Aleppo","image_path":"/8wF3AXsybsoWLQLhkEyG5nrNi0L.jpg","director":"Feras Fayyad","winner":false},{"type":"movie","id":428612,"name":"Strong Island","image_path":"/waXERQjJdXz7iIGMlSrP8OGzSE8.jpg","director":"Yance F